tion gives roughly 10^3 GPU-hours per training run; with LR search (\u22486 short runs at 20% data) and 3 seeds, the full protocol is plausibly 2\u20134\u00d710^4 GPU-hours \u2014 i.e., multi-node, multi-week. This environment (224 CPUs, no GPU, no network) executes none of it.\nPre-registered cut order under pressure: (1) B1/B2 budget arms (curves survive from logged budget statistics); (2) uncleaned-corpus leak sensitivity run; (3) Instruct-init sensitivity pair; (4) seeds 3\u21922\u21921; (5) OOD secondary sets (drop AQuA, TabMWP first); LR grid narrows before seeds never go below 1; A3 control is evaluation-only and is never cut.\nIf only the primary comparison is affordable, the design still delivers: practitioners' A1-vs-A2-vs-A3 with symmetric LR selection, cleaned data, primary endpoint with CIs, item-level paired tests, and measured update-budget statistics \u2014 losing only the extra trained points on the budget axes, the initialization and leakage sensitivity checks, and training-variance estimation.\n\nD7. WHAT WOULD FALSIFY OR WEAKEN THE CONCLUSION\nA BAdam win is falsified or discounted if: (i) LoRA's LR curve is still rising at its grid top or BAdam's best sits at its boundary \u2014 an optimizer-tuning artifact (mitigated by the symmetric grid and boundary rule, but detectable by reporting full LR curves); (ii) the win concentrates entirely in the contamination-exposed stratum; (iii) the win vanishes once unextractable-format outputs are handled, i.e., it is format compliance rather than math correctness; (iv) with multiple seeds the seed spread swallows the gap; (v) GSM8K and MATH disagree in direction \u2014 reported, not averaged away silently (the averaged endpoint decides the formal claim, the disaggregation reports the caveat); (vi) the OOD transfer table reverses the ranking, suggesting benchmark-specific overfitting. A BAdam loss equally falsifies H1 and is reported with the same disaggregations.\n\nCONSTRAINTS HONORED: no experiment was run